
  Change the parent branch worktrees are rebased onto: the next `wtm sync` rebases them onto it.
  Only the meta record changes: no branch, commit nor file moves. Their children follow them.
  Without arguments, the worktree you stand in moves; the wizard asks which worktrees to move
  and onto which branch, a local branch or origin/<branch>.

  A worktree cannot sit under itself: a parent that is one of the worktrees moved, or sits under
  one of them, is refused. Never the main worktree, the base branch's, one on no branch or one
  wtm did not create. A worktree already on the parent is left as it is.

  Usage:
    wtm-next reparent [worktree...] [flags]

  Examples:
    # Move the worktree you stand in
    wtm reparent --to main

    # Several at once, no prompts
    wtm reparent feat/b feat/c --to feat/a --yes

    # See the plan first, then apply exactly that plan
    wtm reparent feat/b --to main --dry-run
    wtm reparent feat/b --to main --expect-fingerprint <hash>

    # For a script or an agent, with the v2 JSON envelope
    wtm reparent feat/b --to main --yes --output json

  Flags:
        --ask                         Ask again the questions this repository remembers an answer to, to change or forget it
    -n, --dry-run                     Show the plan and its fingerprint, apply nothing
        --expect-fingerprint string   Apply only if the facts still have this fingerprint, the one --dry-run printed
    -h, --help                        help for reparent
        --output string               Output format: text or json (default "text")
        --to string                   The branch the worktrees are rebased onto from now on: a local branch, or origin/<branch>
    -y, --yes                         Run unattended: no question, no confirmation (--to required; the worktree you stand in unless worktrees are named)

  Global Flags:
    -q, --quiet   Silence human output; errors and the exit code are unaffected, and --output json still emits its document

